{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"CLSA-2026-1789636275","published":"2026-09-17T09:11:26Z","modified":"2026-10-26T09:32:02.520634539Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-11972","CVE-2026-9669"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-11972, CVE-2026-9669","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: quadratic parse time in the tarfile module when a\n     streaming archive declares an offset past the end of the stream\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-11972.patch: stop the forward-seek loop in\n       _Stream.seek() as soon as read() returns no data, in Lib/tarfile.py,\n       so a crafted mode=\"r|\" archive can no longer keep the parser reading\n       an exhausted stream.\n     - CVE-2026-11972\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: out-of-bounds write when a bz2 decompressor is reused\n     after a decompression error\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-9669.patch: record the libbzip2 error in the\n       BZ2Decompressor object and refuse any further decompress() call with\n       ValueError, in Modules/_bz2module.c, so retrying with the same object\n       can no longer re-enter BZ2_bzDecompress() on a bz_stream left in an\n       invalid internal state.\n     - CVE-2026-9669","affected":[{"package":{"name":"idle-python3.5","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/idle-python3.5?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:3.5.2-2ubuntu0~16.04.13+tuxcare.els30"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu16.04els/CLSA-2026-1789636275.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libpython3.5","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/libpython3.5?distro=ubuntu-16.04"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:3.5.2-2ubuntu0~16.04.13+tuxcare.els30"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/ubuntu16.04els/CLSA-2026-1789636275.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libpython3.5-dev","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Ubuntu:16.04","purl"